  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="plan-2026-09-18 §2">Scope: the file set. EXACTLY these nine files. Tasks 082 and 093 are excluded by decision, not by oversight — do not "helpfully" patch them, and do not treat their exclusion as an error to report.</constraint>
    <constraint source="audit-2026-09-18 + plan-2026-09-18">Scope: trusting the source notes. Both notes UNDER-COUNT the sites per file, and the plan's "Proposed shape" line omits 055 and 056 entirely. Use the notes as a starting inventory, never as a closed one: read each file end to end and repair every occurrence.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §2">Scope: every repaired claim. Code wins. Verify each corrected claim against the actual source file at HEAD before writing it. A claim copied from a note without checking the code is the defect this task exists to remove — reproducing it here would be the eighteenth instance.</constraint>
    <constraint source="plan-2026-09-18 §2 (expected-occurrence discipline)">Scope: verification of each edit. Assert each edit by expected occurrence count, so a miss THROWS rather than silently leaving a stale sentence. After repairing 087/088/089, a grep for the stale sibling numbers in each file MUST return zero: no `080` or `082` in 087, no `081` in 088, no `081` or `082` in 089. Legitimate references (060, 063, 064, 106, 032, 036, 043, 055, 086, 087, 088) must survive untouched.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §7">Scope: status vocabulary. This task changes NO other POML's `&lt;status&gt;`. The nine files stay open; repairing a premise is not completing a task. Setting 115's own status is the only status write.</constraint>
    <constraint source="main-session ownership">Scope: files outside the nine. Do NOT edit `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` or `current-task.md` — the main session owns both. Do not touch anything under `.claude/`. No production file (`src/**`, `tests/**`, `scripts/**`, `docs/**`) is in scope for this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md">Scope: the 054/055/056 reconciliation. The corrected text must say what task 028 actually ruled: a service request IS core, and is NEVER externally grantable. Do not overcorrect into "service request is not core" — that is a different false claim, and the grant table's deliberate omission of a service-request lookup is the evidence for the distinction.</constraint>
    <constraint source="XML validity">Scope: every file written. Each file must remain parseable XML. Escape `&lt;` as `&amp;lt;` inside element text. A prior session shipped six POMLs containing a literal `&amp;lt;?xml` escape in place of the declaration — verify the declaration is a real processing instruction after editing.</constraint>
  </constraints>

