  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Context + rigor declaration. Read all nine files end to end plus the two source notes. Build the per-file site inventory from the FILES, using the notes only as a cross-check — record where your inventory exceeds theirs.</step>
    <step order="1">Verify each corrected claim against its cited source at HEAD: the `appsettings*` inventory (036), `notes/task-028-service-request-root.md` plus the project CLAUDE.md three-root rule (054/055/056), the task titles of 080/081/082/086/087/088 (the renumbering), `DriveItemOperations.ListChildrenAsync` and the `ClientSupplied` allow-list (094), and `DocumentLinkFields.All` in `Models.cs` (095). Any mismatch with the audit's description fires the escalation below.</step>
    <step order="2">Repair the three numbering files (087, 088, 089) in every element — gate, goal, prompt, background, dependency, constraint, step, knowledge, justification, escalation — then run the residual-reference greps from the constraint and confirm each returns zero.</step>
    <step order="3">Repair the retired-premise chain (054, then 055, then 056) so the binding elements carry the task-028 ruling rather than only `&lt;notes&gt;`; repair 036's two `appsettings.json` sites; add 094's record-keyed-probe requirement; correct 095's two false absences and the workassignment-pair claim.</step>
    <step order="4">Verify: `pwsh scripts/Validate-TaskPoml.ps1 projects/unified-access-control-r2/tasks` exits 0; `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1` exits 0; every edited file parses as XML; a diff review confirms no `&lt;status&gt;` element and no file outside the nine changed.</step>
    <step order="5">Write the repair record to `projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-115-task-file-accuracy-repair.md`: per file, the wrong sentence, the corrected sentence, and the source that settled it. Report the sites found beyond the notes' inventory so the next audit knows both notes under-counted.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a cited source line no longer matches the audit's description — the source file moved or was refactored, the line region changed meaning, or the claimed defect is not actually present at HEAD — STOP on that file and report the discrepancy with the evidence. Do NOT write the audit's version of the claim over a file that has since become correct, and do not silently skip the file. The audit has already been found under-stated twice; it can equally be over-stated on a specific line.</trigger>
    <trigger>If repairing 054/055/056 requires deciding what the requester MAY DO to their own service request's to-dos (the open ISS-003 / #964 product question), STOP at the premise repair. Removing the retired fourth-root premise is in scope; choosing the replacement scope is the owner's decision and must not be improvised into the file.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/unified-access-control-r2/tasks/{036,054,055,056,087,088,089,094,095}-*.poml (repaired instruction text)</output>
