  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">036 — no reference to `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/appsettings.json` remains (neither the `&lt;file role="modify"&gt;` entry nor step 1's "appsettings.json comments"); the option's documented home is a file that exists at HEAD.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">054 — no BINDING element (title, prompt, goal, steps, acceptance criteria) asserts an accessible-service-request root set or an extension of the grant allow-list to `sprk_servicerequest`; the file states the task-028 ruling that a service request is core but never externally grantable, and CallerPrincipal composes exactly three externally-grantable root sets.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">055 — the `&lt;gate&gt;`, `&lt;dependency task="054"&gt;` and step-1 text no longer presuppose a "fourth root set"; the inheritance term is described over the roots that actually exist.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">056 — the `&lt;goal&gt;`, the `&lt;constraint source="project"&gt;` ("four composed core root sets"), step 2 ("054's root set") and the background ("054 added the fourth") no longer assert a service-request root set as a scope dimension.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">087 — every `080` now reads `086` (table + vocabulary) and every `082` now reads `088` (replay), across gate, goal, background, dependency, knowledge, step 3 and justification; a grep for `080` and for `082` in the file returns zero; `&lt;deps&gt;` still reads 086, 060, 063, 064, 106.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">088 — every `081` now reads `087` (event backbone), across gate, prompt, goal, background, dependency, constraint, step 1 and justification; a grep for `081` in the file returns zero; `&lt;deps&gt;` still reads 087, 032, 036, 043, 055, 064.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">089 — the `&lt;gate&gt;` reads "requires 087 + 088", the two `&lt;dependency&gt;` elements name 087 (event hooks) and 088 (replay + versioning), and the background and escalation cite the same; a grep for `081` and for `082` in the file returns zero, so the file no longer blocks on task 082, the live caller-identity census.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">094 — the file states that the pre-flight probe MUST be record-keyed `(entity, recordId, name)` with the container server-resolved, and that `ListChildrenAsync` is drive-keyed and therefore cannot be reused as-is without reintroducing the `ClientSupplied` shape task 083 deleted (which `SpeWriteSinkContainerProvenanceGuardTests` pins at zero entries).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">095 — the background no longer claims `sprk_document` lacks a `sprk_todo` or `contact` lookup; it names `sprk_relatedtodo` and `sprk_relatedcontact` as existing, `account` as the only genuine absence, and Document-to-WorkAssignment as a pair rather than one.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1` exits 0 after the repair (POML statuses still agree with their index markers).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No POML `&lt;status&gt;` element was changed by this task — the nine repaired files remain open, verified by diff; 115's own status is the only status write.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`pwsh scripts/Validate-TaskPoml.ps1 projects/unified-access-control-r2/tasks` exits 0, every edited file parses as XML, and the diff touches no file outside the nine plus this task's notes file.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>NOT STARTED. Wave 0 of the 2026-09-18 remediation plan — runs BEFORE any execution task, because nine of the files an executor would load are wrong in a way that survives a green build.

Scope arithmetic, recorded because the two source notes disagree: the audit's headline count is 8; the plan's §2 table has 9 ROWS but two of them (082, 093) are excluded as rescopes, and its "Proposed shape" line names only 7 files. The nine IN-SCOPE files are 036, 054, 055, 056, 087, 088, 089, 094, 095 — 055 and 056 belong because they carry 054's retired premise in BINDING elements (gate, goal, constraint, dependency, steps), not merely "by inheritance" as the audit's §3 item 3 describes them.</notes>

